@dodio Thank you so much for your recognition and encouragement — it truly means a lot to me. You’re absolutely right: in today’s Web3 environment, using CKB for payments isn’t an ideal choice due to its high price volatility, which makes it unsuitable for real-world business scenarios. Stablecoins like USDI are clearly more appropriate for payment use cases.
In fact, Fiber already supports UDT payments, including USDI. I’m considering using USDI in my next project demo to better reflect practical application needs.
Regarding the ISO 15118 “Plug & Charge” protocol, I haven’t explored it in depth yet, but I’ll definitely look into it further to see how it could be integrated into future designs. Thank you again for your valuable suggestions — they’re incredibly helpful for shaping the direction of this project.
